// The high-level client: the same calls as @client, answering domain types.
//
// Strictly a layer. Every method here is its @client counterpart plus one
// extraction step, and `Api::client` hands the low-level client back for
// everything this package does not wrap -- the 260-odd methods with no typed
// call at all, a field @model does not carry, the raw JSON.
//
// A wrapper struct rather than more methods on `Client`, for two reasons.
// MoonBit only allows a method in the package that defines its type, so this
// could not extend `Client` from here even if it wanted to. And keeping them
// apart lets a method here take the SAME name and arguments as the one it
// wraps, differing only in what it answers -- `client.users_info(...)` gives
// you an `ApiResponse`, `api.users_info(...)` gives you a `User`.
import {
  "marianoguerra/slack/api",
  "marianoguerra/slack/blocks",
  "marianoguerra/slack/client",
  "marianoguerra/slack/model",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}

// No test block: every method here is `async`, an `async test` needs
// moonbitlang/async, and this module does not have it. They live in
// ext/test/highlevel, against @mock -- which is the right place anyway, since
// what is worth testing is a whole call and not an extraction step.
